From: Thomas Cherryhomes <thom.cherryhomes@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] 5200: analog sticks from a platform's Atari_POT

With PLATFORM_POT the 5200 branch of INPUT_Frame reads Atari_POT(2*port) and
(2*port+1) first, as the Dreamcast port does, and falls back to the digital
STICK only while both sit at the centre (114).
---
diff --git a/src/input.c b/src/input.c
index c0694f4..7f2132e 100644
--- a/src/input.c
+++ b/src/input.c
@@ -632,7 +632,7 @@ void INPUT_Frame(void)
 	}
 	else {
 		for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
-#ifdef DREAMCAST
+#if defined(DREAMCAST) || defined(PLATFORM_POT)
 			/* first get analog js data */
 			POKEY_POT_input[2 * i] = Atari_POT(2 * i);         /* x */
 			POKEY_POT_input[2 * i + 1] = Atari_POT(2 * i + 1); /* y */
